            "text": "[Compacted context summary; archived messages were replaced locally]\n\n# Compacted context summary\n\n## Active goal\nPolish multi-conversation UX in the three ai_exec viewers; support parallel multi-chat runners without changing ae.py. Keep context manageable via compaction skill.\n\n## Workspace / launch\n- Root: C:\\Users\\12159\\Desktop\\ai_exec\n- Active viewer: responses/viewer.py (equivalents: chat_completions/, messages/)\n- Launch: ./view.vbs -> pythonw viewer.py\n- Active transcript: responses/input.json (pointer .ae_active_input)\n- ae.py: unchanged; reads Path(argv[1]) only\n- Compaction skill: responses/skills/context_compaction\n\n## Multi-chat (sessions) — done earlier\n- list/create/select/rename/delete; default protected\n- Auto-name 新对话 / 新对话2...; copy default config, clear transcript\n- Active chat via .ae_active_input\n- Settled rail: fixed top-left, transparent, mainly '+'\n\n## Parallel multi-chat tasks — done (ae.py untouched)\n- Per-chat runners: _runners[chat_id] + .ae_runners/<transcript-filename>.pid\n- start_process(chat_id, input_file) / stop_process(chat_id) / stop_all_processes()\n- /api/send only blocks if THAT chat is running; switch does NOT stop others\n- stop/retract only affect current chat; delete stops that chat's runner\n- Env for children: AE_RUNNER=1, AE_INPUT_FILE, AE_CONVERSATION_ID (compaction still kills own parent via getppid)\n- Chat list shows running badge (绿点 +「运行中」); poll refreshes list ~2.5s when any running\n\n## Bugfixes after parallel work\n1. Rename while running FORBIDDEN (ae.py holds argv path → split-brain). Message: 对话运行中，请先停止再重命名\n2. PID files keyed by transcript filename (avoid \"a b\" vs \"a_b\" collision)\n3. Switch chat: reset running UI; syncRunningFromCache only UPGRADES to running (poll owns downgrade)\n4. Per-chat drafts: localStorage ae-draft:<chatId>\n5. create_chat template read retries (8x) under concurrent runner writes\n6. stop_process resolves pid before reading registry entry\n\n## Recent UX polish\n1. Rail density by chat count:\n   - 0–1 chats: only '+' (html.chat-solo-rail, compact width)\n   - 2–3: list, no search\n   - ≥4: list + search\n   - ≤640px viewport: still only '+' (unchanged)\n2. Delete chat: no confirm() dialog; direct delete + toast\n\n## Modified files (keep in sync)\n- responses/viewer.py\n- chat_completions/viewer.py\n- messages/viewer.py\nDo NOT edit ae.py unless user asks.\n\n## Verification habits\n- py_compile all three viewers\n- node --check on inline JS blocks\n- Temp-dir functional tests for runners/rename/pid when touching process logic\n- Avoid long browser/Playwright downloads unless user asks\n- Restart via ./view.vbs to load viewer edits\n\n## Architecture notes / limits\n- Three viewers still highly duplicated; extract shared core only if user requests\n- Parallel ae.py share cwd=ROOT; relative writes to input.json can hit default chat — skills should use AE_INPUT_FILE\n- No per-row stop in rail; user switches into chat then stops\n- Markdown stack: marked 11.1.1, DOMPurify 3.1.6, highlight.js 11.9.0 CDN\n\n## Exact next task\nWait for user's next request. Prefer targeted checks; do not revisit settled rail chrome unless asked."
